TASK-186.5 runtime harness: dev mode's per-site switch in the address bar
popover, the sidebar rows following it at once in two windows, the Private
window's choice staying out of the database, and the new popover button.
Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task186-5-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # $SITE/remote.html and $SITE/app.html, each a <title> + <h1>:
    python3 -m http.server 8865 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory "$SITE" &
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify1865 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8865 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # a watcher reads only the new lines of $OUT/verify.log every 0.2 s and
    # runs `screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber> $OUT/<name>.png` for each
    # "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>" line. The harness waits for each
    # requested PNG before its next step (on a machine at load ~1000 a
    # timer-only schedule shot states up to 9 s late). Wait for "done"
    # (about 55 s), then kill that pid and the server.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task186-5-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    rm -r -- ~/Library/Application\ Support/DetourVerify1865

The "remote" site is kubernetes.docker.internal:8865: /etc/hosts maps it to
127.0.0.1 (Docker Desktop's entry), so the 127.0.0.1-bound server answers it
with no network, and it is not local by `isLocalDevelopmentURL`. The local
site is localhost:8865. Window 2 is `createNewWindow(showing:)` on the same
space; the Private window is `createNewIncognitoWindow()`. Switches are driven
with performClick on the popover's "Dev mode for this site" NSSwitch; each
click logs every row in the affected windows in the same run-loop turn
("immediately"), before any capture.

